    "type": "question",
    "label": "50",
    "prompt": "Show that\n$$\\binom{n+2}{k}=\\binom{n}{k}+2\\binom{n}{k-1}+\\binom{n}{k-2}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": " $\\displaystyle\\binom{n+2}{k}=\\binom{n}{k}+2\\binom{n}{k-1}+\\binom{n}{k-2}$.\n\nApply Pascal's identity twice and collect the two identical middle terms.",
      "worked": "Apply Pascal's identity twice:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\binom{n+2}{k}&=\\binom{n+1}{k}+\\binom{n+1}{k-1}\\\\\n\\binom{n+2}{k}&=\\binom{n}{k}+\\binom{n}{k-1}+\\binom{n}{k-1}+\\binom{n}{k-2}\\\\\n\\binom{n+2}{k}&=\\binom{n}{k}+2\\binom{n}{k-1}+\\binom{n}{k-2}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
